* Data is divided into two parts:
    - numerical data
    - categorical data
* Categorical data is of two types  as well:
    - Nominal (Categories have no relationships or order among them or say have equal weightage. E.g: state:Karachi, Islamabad)
    - Ordinal (Categories have some relationships or order among them. E.g: grades in school so like grade A > grade B)

* Techniques for Encoding categorical data:
    - Ordinal encoding (use for ordinal data)
    - One hot encoding (use for nominal data)
    - Label encoding (similar to ordinal encoding)

* If we have any column in our predictors(input data) that is ordinal categorical data, use ordinal encoding.
* If the ordinal categorical data is in our target coulmn, use label encoder.

 Ordinal encoding:
    - It assigns each category a specific number.
    - As it is ordinal specify which category to assign the highet value, and so on.
    - Or it itself assigns value as it iterate through data.
