One hot encoding:
    Case - 01 : Nominal data
        - foreg blue, red, green
        - It divides the categories in 3 coulmns(dummy variables) and give 1/0 value accordingly.
     Dummy variable trap: always remove any one of the columns, i.e. if like there were three categories = 3 column, make 2 column.
        - why bcz of multicolinearity
     Multi colinearity: In ML columns must be independent of eachother, in above example if we made 3 columns we canfind the relation that in a row if we add the values of 3 columns, it equates to 1. Such kind relation create obstacles in linear models.
    
    Case - 02 : Too many categories
        - In such scenario take the most frequent values and classify all left as others.

